From 43c7aede221ea9f6312e3981ad12b7dfe182bc03 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Neil Cheng <Neil.Cheng@quantatw.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 17:20:02 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] platform-mc: NumericSensor: fix rebase of useMetricInterface
 removal

After rebasing onto upstream 3269cd16dc31 ("platform-mc: add support
for sensor unit bits"), the PLDM_SENSOR_UNIT_BITS case in
setSensorUnit() still assigned `useMetricInterface = true`. That
member was removed by the cherry-picked Gerrit 87817 patch, so the
build fails and the bits case never set its metric unit.

Replace the stale assignment with `sensorUnit = MetricUnit::Bytes`,
matching how the other metric units are handled in the same switch.

This is a local rebase fix on top of Gerrit 87817 and was not raised
as a review comment on Gerrit.

Signed-off-by: Neil Cheng <Neil.Cheng@quantatw.com>
---
 platform-mc/numeric_sensor.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/platform-mc/numeric_sensor.cpp b/platform-mc/numeric_sensor.cpp
index e3595db..bae88a4 100644
--- a/platform-mc/numeric_sensor.cpp
+++ b/platform-mc/numeric_sensor.cpp
@@ -173,7 +173,7 @@ bool NumericSensor::setSensorUnit(uint8_t baseUnit)
             break;
         case PLDM_SENSOR_UNIT_BITS:
             sensorNameSpace = "/xyz/openbmc_project/metric/bytes/";
-            useMetricInterface = true;
+            sensorUnit = MetricUnit::Bytes;
             break;
         default:
             return false;
-- 
